__pycache__/
# Secrets. The provider probe reads credentials from the environment or from
# a local .env; neither may ever be committed (docs/v4/08_DEPLOYMENT.md §4).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
mawos.db
ml/models/*.joblib
ml/data/*.csv
# evaluation/results/ IS tracked. A result that is not version controlled
# cannot be cited -- v2 ignored this whole tree, so none of its published
# numbers were ever committed, and the P0.5 gate output was briefly in the
# same state. An allowlist was tried first and failed the moment a new
# results directory appeared, so the rule is inverted: everything is kept
# except scratch artifacts.
#
# The subdirectories mean different things and must never be conflated:
#   v2_historical/ - what v2 originally reported, preserved unmodified
#   v2_frozen/     - the same system re-measured under PROTOCOL.md
#   v3_llm/        - frozen-protocol model captures
#   v3_gates/      - pre-registered gate and sweep decisions
evaluation/results/**/_scratch.db
# R0.5 probe resume artifact: pure scratch. Every record it holds is also
# embedded in the tracked r05_provider.json, which is the citable evidence.
evaluation/results/**/_r05_checkpoint.json
fl/results/
.venv/
venv/

# ITC-2007 harness: third-party validator source/binary is fetched, never
# vendored (evaluation/itc2007/build.py records its URL and sha256), and
# the competition instances are not ours to redistribute.
evaluation/itc2007/vendor/
evaluation/itc2007/instances/*.ctt

# Local DB snapshots taken before risky migrations. `mawos.db` was already
# ignored; the dated backups are the same file under another name and are
# ~30 MB each, so they must never enter history.
mawos.db.*

# Node dependencies, wherever they appear.
node_modules/

# A teammate's separate Next.js/Postgres reference app. Untouched and NOT
# integrated into MAWOS -- it is here only because its live-trace UI inspired
# `backend/app/scheduler_live.py` (CLAUDE.md). It carries its own node_modules
# and is tracked in its own repo, so it is not vendored into this history.
# Reverse by deleting this line if the team decides to fold it in.
teacher-erp-with-timetable-simulation/
